<paper_information>
<title>{title}</title>
<authors>{authors}</authors>
<abstract>{abstract}</abstract>
</paper_information>

<sections>
{context}
</sections>

<goal_setting>
{goal}
</goal_setting>

<selected_section_indices>
{selected_section_indices}
</selected_section_indices>

<sufficiency_check>
{sufficiency_check}
</sufficiency_check>

<task>
To achieve the objective described in the goal_setting tag, you will perform the research task: "{task}".
You are currently reading the paper contained in the paper_information tag.
Based on the content included in the sections tag, output the section numbers that should be read in order to execute the research task.
Output the section numbers separated by commas.

Example:
1,3,4

You may select up to {max_sections} sections.
</task>

You must strictly follow the content enclosed in the rules tag below.

<rules>
- Do not specify any section numbers included in the selected_section_indices tag.
- Select section numbers by referring to the content described in the sufficiency_check tag.
- Output multiple section numbers separated by commas.
- Do not include any spaces.
</rules>
